        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127193,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cellular angiolipoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127194,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiolipomas most frequently involve the extremities, followed by the trunk, but a wide range of sites may be involved, including the head and neck, breast, deep soft tissue, and organs {13716236; 28662999; 21087987; 20197228; 32972286}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127195,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with angiolipomas usually present with multiple small, painful subcutaneous nodules {30858718; 8436643}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127196,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiolipomas typically arise in children and young adults, with a male predominance. Approximately 5% of cases are familial with an autosomal dominant mode of inheritance {2706802}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127197,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127198,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The precise pathogenesis is unknown, but angiolipomas have frequent mutations in <em>PRKD2</em> and <em>PIK3CA</em>. It is thought that altered <em>PRKD2</em> in adipocytes probably stimulates angiogenesis {28139834}. <em>PIK3CA</em> mutations disrupt the PI3K/AKT signalling pathway. In mouse models, alterations of this signalling pathway can cause spontaneous development of lipomatous tumours {32662895; 26317218}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127199,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiolipomas are usually encapsulated yellow to reddish nodules.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127200,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiolipomas have varying proportions of mature adipocytes and clusters of thin-walled capillaries, often with intravascular thrombi containing numerous platelets, embedded in hyalinized stroma with spindled cells. The vascular component is more prominent at the periphery of the tumour. Cellular angiolipomas are predominantly composed of the vascular component, with few fat cells {22935891}.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>Spindle cell lipoma lacks clusters of capillaries and has ropy collagen bundles. Kaposi sarcoma is composed of spindled cells with slit-like vascular spaces and is immunoreactive for KSHV/HHV8. The vessels of angiosarcoma have complex architecture, and the tumour cells have nuclear atypia. Intramuscular haemangiomas have more-variable vessels, rather than only clusters of capillaries.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127201,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127202,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127203,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> tender, often multiple subcutaneous nodules; mature fat with a variable number of capillary vessels; fibrin microthrombi.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127204,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127205,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 225,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiolipomas are benign and typically do not recur.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:45:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]